  "description": "UtcMilliTime for .NET 8.0 + .NET 10+ provides Unix time milliseconds (Int64) timestamps, similar to JavaScript's Date.now(), with cross-platform support and NTP synchronization.\n\n      Version 3 introduces thread safety across the Clock singleton and adds NowNonce() — a 12-byte value (8-byte timestamp + 4-byte entropy) designed for cryptographic use cases such as nonces in encryption and JWT handling.",
